  "details": "World hopping with friends can be frustrating and disjointed due to loading screens. Players load in at different speeds, with those using higher-end hardware awkwardly waiting for others, while those with slower storage face the same issue. This interrupts the group dynamic as everyone loads in separately.\n\nTo address this, I propose a seamless portal system, allowing players to place a \"seamless portal\" that transports everyone to a shared space. While people are loading, they can continue chatting, making the experience feel more cohesive. Additionally, this would give world creators more creative freedom for spawn points and enhance the overall experience by eliminating jarring loading screens from 2014.",
